  "caveat": "A float is never exactly on a grid cell at the grid time, so part of every gap is collocation mismatch. The TIGHT table is the honest lower bound.",
  "caveat_statistical": "The 95% interval is bootstrapped on the REANALYSIS RMSE only; our model's RMSE is treated as a fixed stored number because per-profile model residuals are not saved. A fully paired test would widen the intervals, which would move verdicts TOWARD 'indistinguishable', never away from it. So the large-margin 'we add error' verdicts at 20-75 m are safe, while the marginal ones (300 m) and the 1000 m 'better' verdict are the ones that might not survive a paired test. Say this if asked."
